# Keeps frontend/public/ present in git.
#
# The directory is empty by design — the create-next-app sample SVGs were
# removed and the app icon lives at app/icon.svg — but Dockerfile line 25 does
# `COPY --from=builder /app/public ./public`, which fails the image build if the
# path is absent. Git does not track empty directories, so without this file a
# fresh clone (CI, or the VM after `git reset --hard`) cannot build the frontend.
